<header class="ref-head yr-head"><p class="cty-kicker">Year by year · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p><h1 class="research-title">1943</h1><p class="ref-lede">1943 in world history: 34 events, 9 births, 15 deaths, 3 works, 8 states founded and 5 that came to an end. 719 recorded states existed that year.</p></header>
<nav class="ref-letters yr-near" aria-label="Nearby years"><a href="/years/1939">1939</a><a href="/years/1940">1940</a><a href="/years/1941">1941</a><a href="/years/1942">1942</a><a href="/years/1943" aria-current="page">1943</a><a href="/years/1944">1944</a><a href="/years/1945">1945</a><a href="/years/1946">1946</a><a href="/years/1947">1947</a></nav>
<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-14">14 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Roosevelt and Churchill meet at Casablanca</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/casablanca">Casablanca</a> Conference agreed to invade <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a> and intensify the bombing of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. At its close Roosevelt announced that the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a> would accept only unconditional surrender.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-15">15 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The Pentagon is completed in Arlington, Virginia</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Built in just 16 months, the five-sided headquarters of the US War <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">Department</a> was dedicated. With some 6.5 million square feet of floor space, it was the world's largest office building.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-18">18 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Soviet forces open a land corridor into besieged Leningrad</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">In Operation Iskra, Soviet troops linked up south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-ladoga">Lake Ladoga</a>, creating a narrow corridor into Leningrad after 16 months of siege. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naval-blockade">blockade</a> was finally lifted in January 1944.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-23">23 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">British Eighth Army captures Tripoli</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Montgomery's troops entered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tripoli">Tripoli</a>, three months after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/el-alamein">El Alamein</a>, as Rommel's forces retreated into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tunisia">Tunisia</a>. It ended <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>'s North African empire.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tunisia">Tunisia</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tripoli">Tripoli</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/february-2">2 February</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">German Sixth Army's last units surrender at Stalingrad</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The final German forces in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volgograd">Stalingrad</a>'s northern pocket laid down their arms. Some 91,000 were taken prisoner, and the defeat marked a turning point of the war on the Eastern Front.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/february-18">18 February</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Hans and Sophie Scholl arrested in Munich</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The siblings of the White Rose resistance group were caught distributing anti-Nazi leaflets at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/munich">Munich</a> University. They were tried and guillotined four days later.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/march-2">2 March</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Battle of the Bismarck Sea begins</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">American and Australian aircraft attacked a Japanese convoy bound for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-guinea">New Guinea</a>, sinking all eight transports and four destroyers over three days. About 3,000 Japanese troops died.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guinea">Guinea</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/smolensk" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/smolensk.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/april-13">13 April</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Germany announces discovery of the Katyń graves</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin">Berlin</a> radio reported mass graves of Polish officers in the Katyń Forest near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/smolensk">Smolensk</a>. They had been shot by the Soviet <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nkvd">NKVD</a> in 1940, a crime <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a> denied until 1990.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/smolensk">Smolensk</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/april-16">16 April</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Albert Hofmann experiences the effects of LSD by accident</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Working at Sandoz in Basel, chemist Albert Hofmann absorbed a trace of LSD and felt its effects. Three days later, on 19 April, he took a deliberate dose to test it.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/warsaw" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/warsaw.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/april-19">19 April</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Warsaw Ghetto Uprising begins</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Jewish fighters resisted German troops sent to deport the ghetto's remaining inhabitants to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treblinka-extermination-camp">Treblinka</a>. They held out for nearly a month in the largest Jewish revolt of the war.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warsaw">Warsaw</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/july-4">4 July</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Polish leader Władysław Sikorski dies in a crash at Gibraltar</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">General Sikorski, prime minister of the Polish government-in-exile, was killed when his aircraft crashed seconds after take-off from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gibraltar">Gibraltar</a>. His death removed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a>' most respected Polish voice at a critical moment.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gibraltar">Gibraltar</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/july-12">12 July</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Soviet and German tanks clash at Prokhorovka</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Soviet tank armies counter-attacked the SS Panzer Corps at Prokhorovka, one of the largest tank battles in history. The Soviets lost heavily, but the German offensive at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kursk">Kursk</a> was halted.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/september-3">3 September</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Italy secretly signs an armistice with the Allies</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Italian and Allied officers signed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armistice-of-cassibile">Armistice of Cassibile</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a>, the same day British troops landed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/calabria">Calabria</a>. When it was announced on 8 September, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> occupied much of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/armistice-of-cassibile" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/armistice-of-cassibile.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/september-3">3 September</a> · Peace</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/armistice-of-cassibile">Armistice of Cassibile</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Armistice of Cassibile was the armistice between Italy and the Allies, signed secretly on 3 September 1943 at an Allied camp near Cassibile in Sicily and announced on 8 September.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/september-8">8 September</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Italy's armistice with the Allies is announced</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dwight-d-eisenhower">Eisenhower</a> broadcast news of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>'s surrender. German troops quickly disarmed the Italian army and occupied much of the country, which became a battleground for 20 months.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/october-13">13 October</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Italy declares war on Germany</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Five weeks after its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armistice-of-11-november-1918">armistice</a> with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pietro-badoglio">Pietro Badoglio</a>'s Italian government declared war on its former <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/axis-powers">Axis</a> partner. German forces nonetheless occupied northern and central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> until 1945.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/november-28">28 November</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Churchill, Roosevelt and Stalin meet in Tehran</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The 'Big Three' met together for the first time at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tehran">Tehran</a> Conference. They committed to a cross-Channel invasion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> in 1944 and discussed the shape of post-war <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/cairo-conference" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cairo-conference.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/cairo-conference">Cairo Conference</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Cairo Conference was a meeting held in Cairo in November 1943 between Franklin D.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Campaign</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/allied-invasion-of-sicily">Allied invasion of Sicily</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Allied invasion of Sicily was the Second World War campaign in 1943 in which British, American and Canadian forces landed on and captured Sicily.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-kursk">Battle of Kursk</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Kursk was fought on the Eastern Front in July and August 1943, when Germany attacked the Soviet salient around Kursk in Operation Citadel.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/german-occupation-of-italy" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/german-occupation-of-italy.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/german-occupation-of-italy">German occupation of Italy</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The German occupation of Italy began in 1943, after Italy signed an armistice with the Allies and German forces took control of much of the country.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/operation-gomorrah" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/operation-gomorrah.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Campaign</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/operation-gomorrah">Operation Gomorrah</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Operation Gomorrah was a series of British and American air raids on Hamburg in late July and early August 1943.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-leros" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-leros.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-leros">Battle of Leros</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Leros was fought in November 1943 on the Aegean island of Leros, which British and Italian troops had held since Italy's armistice in September.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-tarawa" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-tarawa.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-tarawa">Battle of Tarawa</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Tarawa was fought from 20 to 23 November 1943 on Betio, an islet of Tarawa atoll in the Gilbert Islands, when United States Marines stormed a strongly fortified Japanese garrison.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Campaign</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/dodecanese-campaign">Dodecanese campaign</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Dodecanese campaign was a British attempt in late 1943 to seize the Italian-held Dodecanese islands in the Aegean after Italy's armistice with the Allies.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/khatyn-massacre">Khatyn massacre</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Khatyn massacre was the destruction of the village of Khatyn in Belarus by a German auxiliary police battalion and SS troops on 22 March 1943.</p></div></li></ol></section>
